      `the commission of the offence resulted in bodily harm to, or the death of, more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.22(a) the court shall consider that the offence resulted in bodily harm to, or the death of, more than one person` MEANS
    IF `the commission of the offence resulted in bodily harm to, or the death of, more than one person`
    THEN `the sentence is for an offence under any of sections 320.13 to 320.18, by s 320.22`
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the commission of the offence resulted in bodily harm to, or the death of, more than one person" (the circumstance of this paragraph is absent)

