-- The duty as a regulative rule: the court MUST consider the circumstances. The text gives no time limit, so none is invented; a trace of it never breaches (see NOTES.md, what the stable binary does not accept).
DECLARE `s 320.22 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 320.22 consider, in addition to any other aggravating circumstances, the circumstances of paragraphs (a) to (g)`

@ref Criminal Code s 320.22 (src:6296-6297)
GIVEN `the sentence is for an offence under any of sections 320.13 to 320.18` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 320.22 action`
`s 320.22 the court shall consider the aggravating circumstances` MEANS
    IF `the sentence is for an offence under any of sections 320.13 to 320.18`
    THEN PARTY `the court`
         MUST `s 320.22 consider, in addition to any other aggravating circumstances, the circumstances of paragraphs (a) to (g)`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court did not consider the aggravating circumstances that section 320.22 names"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- The paragraphs of section 320.22 that apply, as a list of paragraph letters, from the seven answers (the same answers, composed; no rule is restated).
@ref Criminal Code s 320.22 (src:6296-6304)
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      c IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      d IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      e IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      f IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      g IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 320.22 the paragraphs of section 320.22 that apply` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (IF a EQUALS (JUST TRUE) THEN LIST "(a)" ELSE EMPTY),
        (IF b EQUALS (JUST TRUE) THEN LIST "(b)" ELSE EMPTY),
        (IF c EQUALS (JUST TRUE) THEN LIST "(c)" ELSE EMPTY),
        (IF d EQUALS (JUST TRUE) THEN LIST "(d)" ELSE EMPTY),
        (IF e EQUALS (JUST TRUE) THEN LIST "(e)" ELSE EMPTY),
        (IF f EQUALS (JUST TRUE) THEN LIST "(f)" ELSE EMPTY),
        (IF g EQUALS (JUST TRUE) THEN LIST "(g)" ELSE EMPTY))

§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.26: earlier and subsequent offences`

-- 320.26: "In determining, for the purpose of imposing a sentence for an offence under subsection 320.14(1) or 320.15(1), whether the offence is a second, third or subsequent offence, any of the
-- following offences for which the offender was previously convicted is considered to be an earlier offence: (a) an offence under any of subsections 320.14(1) to (3) or section 320.15;
-- or (b) an offence under any of sections 253, 254 and 255, as those sections read ... before the day on which this section comes into force."
-- An offence the list does not name is NOT COVERED ("any of the following ... is considered", with no "only": fork F4); an offence not previously convicted is not an earlier offence (JUST FALSE: fork F5).
-- src:6346 | Earlier and subsequent offences
-- src:6347 | 320.26 In determining, for the purpose of imposing a sentence for an offence under subsection 320.14(1) or 320.15(1), whether the offence is a second, third or subsequent offence, any of the following offences for which the offender was previously convicted is considered to be an earlier offence:
-- src:6348 | (a) an offence under any of subsections 320.14(1) to (3) or section 320.15; or
-- src:6349 | (b) an offence under any of sections 253, 254 and 255, as those sections read from time to time before the day on which this section comes into force.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.26 (src:6346-6349)
GIVEN `the earlier offence` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the offender was previously convicted of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was an offence under a section as that section read from time to time before the day on which section 320.26 comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.26 the offence is considered to be an earlier offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offender was previously convicted of it` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any of the following offences for which the offender was previously convicted is considered to be an earlier offence"
        IF `the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 320.14 AND (sub EQUALS "(1)" OR sub EQUALS "(1)(a)" OR sub EQUALS "(1)(b)" OR sub EQUALS "(1)(c)" OR sub EQUALS "(1)(d)" OR sub EQUALS "(2)" OR sub EQUALS "(3)") THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 320.15 AND (sub EQUALS "(1)" OR sub EQUALS "(2)" OR sub EQUALS "(3)") THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 253 OR `the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 254 OR `the earlier offence`'s `section` EQUALS 255) AND `it was an offence under a section as that section read from time to time before the day on which section 320.26 comes into force` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "any of the following offences for which the offender was previously convicted is considered to be an earlier offence"
    WHERE
        sub MEANS `the earlier offence`'s `subsection`

-- How many earlier offences: the sum of the three counts of the list. The occasion follows: none is a first offence; one is a second; two or more is a subsequent offence ("second, third or subsequent").
@ref Criminal Code s 320.26 (src:6346-6349)
GIVEN `the number of convictions under any of subsections 320.14(1) to (3)` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of convictions under section 320.15` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of convictions under section 253, 254 or 255 as they read before the day on which section 320.26 comes into force` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 320.26 the number of earlier offences` MEANS
    `the number of convictions under any of subsections 320.14(1) to (3)` PLUS `the number of convictions under section 320.15` PLUS `the number of convictions under section 253, 254 or 255 as they read before the day on which section 320.26 comes into force`

@ref Criminal Code s 320.26 (src:6346-6349)
GIVEN `the number of earlier offences` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `s 320.19 occasion`
`s 320.26 the occasion of the offence before the court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of earlier offences` AT MOST 0 THEN `s 320.19 a first offence`
        IF `the number of earlier offences` EQUALS 1 THEN `s 320.19 a second offence`
        OTHERWISE `s 320.19 a subsequent offence`
